# Clear error messages (product UI + API)

Users must instantly know **what failed** and **how to fix it**. Never ship vague copy.

## Forbidden (examples)
- "Unable to complete signup request"
- "Something went wrong"
- "Invalid request"
- "Error" / "Failed" with no field name
- "Incomplete" without saying which field

## Required style
- **Name the field** + **state the rule** (+ short fix when useful).
- English only in product UI (see `ui-english-only`).
- Prefer specific HTTP `code` + clear `message` from API; clients show `message` as-is.

## Common rules — use this exact wording (or tighter)

| Check | Message |
|-------|---------|
| Password length | `Password must be at least 8 characters` |
| Password letter | `Password must contain a letter` |
| Password digit | `Password must contain a number` |
| Password hint (UI helper) | `Min 8 characters · include a letter and a number (e.g. Test1234)` |
| Mobile | `Enter a valid 10-digit mobile` |
| Upline missing | `Enter a valid 10-digit upline mobile` |
| Upline not found | `Distributor / Super Distributor not found for this mobile. Use an active upline number.` |
| Mobile already registered | `This mobile number is already registered. Please log in instead.` |
| Location | `Allow location access before continuing` |
| OTP wrong | `Incorrect OTP` |
| OTP expired | `OTP has expired or was not requested. Please request a new OTP.` |
| Signup OTP (test env) | If `TEST_SIGNUP_OTP_OVERRIDES` is set, UI/dev copy may say fixed OTP e.g. `242424` — never guess; read env/docs |

## Where to apply
- Backend `HttpError` messages + Zod `.message` / refine paths
- Web toasts / field errors
- Mobile `showAlert` / inline validation (`validateStep`)
- Forms: show **helper text under the field** for rules (password, OTP, Aadhaar) before submit — don't wait for a vague modal

## When fixing bugs
If a user hits a vague error, replace it with a field-specific message in the same change — don't only document it.
